            <div xml:id="d501">

                <pb facs="0684" n="570" sameAs="frus:frus1922v02/pg570"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">815.00/2378: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Honduras</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Morales</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tegucigalpa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-07-20T15:00:00-06:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 20, 1922—3
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received July 21—10:10
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>57. Referring to the Department’s telegram of July 19, 7 p.m.<anchor n="17"
                        xml:id="d501-f1"/> The President is very grateful to the Department for the
                    prompt action taken with the Nicaraguan Government. Diplomatic relations will
                    not be severed without first advising the Department. This Government has
                    situation completely under control. No further trouble contemplated and I have
                    kept Legation at Managua fully advised by telegram.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Morales</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
